
# The MAP is derived, and git merges it as TEXT — erasing judgment stamps
# with no conflict and no warning (measured: 62 at once). The driver merges the
# stamps from both sides. Register it with `anchors install-hooks`.
anchors.graph.yaml merge=anchors-map

# The PROGRESS of a plan is marked by whoever delivers, and two branches that
# deliver specs of the same plan mark neighboring checkboxes: git asks for manual
# resolution every time (measured: three PRs in a row, identical resolution in all three).
# The driver merges both sides, and `[x]` beats `[ ]` — unchecking by merge would erase
# a delivery that already happened.
*-progress.md merge=anchors-progress
